{"1-4":{"people":[{"id":"levi-h3878","name":"Levi","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"hanani-h2607j","name":"Hanani","kind":"person","brief":"Returned from exile","count":1,"firstVerse":2},{"id":"hananiah-h2608h","name":"Hananiah","kind":"person","brief":"Returned leader","count":1,"firstVerse":2}],"places":[{"id":"jerusalem-h3389","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":2}],"words":[{"base":"H5975","lemma":"עָמַד","tr":"a·mad","gloss":"to stand: stand","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":521},{"base":"H3389","lemma":"יְרוּשָׁלִַ֫ם, יְרוּשְׁלֵם","tr":"ye·ru·sha·laim","gloss":"Jerusalem","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":643},{"base":"H1817","lemma":"דָּל","tr":"dal","gloss":"door","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":88},{"base":"H1129","lemma":"בָּנָה","tr":"ba·nah","gloss":"to build","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":376},{"base":"H2607","lemma":"חֲנָנִי","tr":"cha·na·ni","gloss":"Hanani","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":11},{"base":"H1002","lemma":"בִּירָה","tr":"bi·rah","gloss":"palace","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":16},{"base":"H2552","lemma":"חָמַם","tr":"cha·mam","gloss":"to warm","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":21},{"base":"H7342","lemma":"רָחָב","tr":"ra·chav","gloss":"Broad","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":21},{"base":"H4929","lemma":"מִשְׁמָר","tr":"mish·mar","gloss":"custody","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":22},{"base":"H2608","lemma":"חֲנַנְיָ֫הוּ","tr":"cha·nan·yah","gloss":"Hananiah","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":29}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"NEH","chapter":1,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Hanani, one of my brothers, arrived with men from Judah. So I questioned them about the remnant of the Jews who had survived the exile, and also about Jerusalem.","from":2},{"book":"PSA","chapter":101,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"My eyes favor the faithful of the land, that they may dwell with me; he who walks in the way of integrity shall minister to me.","from":2},{"book":"MAT","chapter":25,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"His master replied, ‘Well done, good and faithful servant! You have been faithful with a few things; I will put you in charge of many things. Enter into the joy of your master!’","from":2},{"book":"GEN","chapter":42,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"and on the third day he said to them, “I fear God. So do this and you will live:","from":2},{"book":"EXO","chapter":18,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Furthermore, select capable men from among the people—God-fearing, trustworthy men who are averse to dishonest gain. Appoint them over the people as leaders of thousands, of hundreds, of fifties, and of tens.","from":2},{"book":"NUM","chapter":12,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"But this is not so with My servant Moses; he is faithful in all My house.","from":2},{"book":"2SA","chapter":23,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"The God of Israel spoke; the Rock of Israel said to me, ‘He who rules the people with justice, who rules in the fear of God,","from":2},{"book":"1KI","chapter":18,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"and Ahab summoned Obadiah, who was in charge of the palace. (Now Obadiah greatly feared the LORD,","from":2}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"5-7":{"people":[{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":6},{"id":"nebuchadnezzar-h5019","name":"Nebuchadnezzar","kind":"person","brief":"Father of Belshazzar","count":1,"firstVerse":6},{"id":"azariah-h5838x","name":"Azariah","kind":"person","brief":"Returned priest","count":1,"firstVerse":7},{"id":"baanah-h1196i","name":"Baanah","kind":"person","brief":"Returned leader","count":1,"firstVerse":7},{"id":"bigvai-h0902g","name":"Bigvai","kind":"person","brief":"Returned leader","count":1,"firstVerse":7},{"id":"bilshan-h1114","name":"Bilshan","kind":"person","brief":"Returned leader","count":1,"firstVerse":7},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":7},{"id":"joshua-h3091j","name":"Joshua","kind":"person","brief":"A High Priest","count":1,"firstVerse":7},{"id":"mispar-h4558","name":"Mispar","kind":"person","brief":"Returned from exile","count":1,"firstVerse":7},{"id":"mordecai-h4782g","name":"Mordecai","kind":"person","brief":"Returned leader","count":1,"firstVerse":7},{"id":"nahamani-h5167","name":"Nahamani","kind":"person","brief":"Returned from exile","count":1,"firstVerse":7},{"id":"nehemiah-h5166g","name":"Nehemiah","kind":"person","brief":"Returned leader","count":1,"firstVerse":7},{"id":"reelaiah-h7480","name":"Reelaiah","kind":"person","brief":"Returned leader","count":1,"firstVerse":7},{"id":"rehum-h7348a","name":"Rehum","kind":"person","brief":"Returned leader","count":1,"firstVerse":7},{"id":"zerubbabel-h2216","name":"Zerubbabel","kind":"person","brief":"Governor","count":1,"firstVerse":7}],"places":[{"id":"babylon-h0894","name":"Babylon","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":6},{"id":"jerusalem-h3389","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":6}],"words":[{"base":"H1114","lemma":"בִּלְשָׁן","tr":"bil·shan","gloss":"Bilshan","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H3188","lemma":"יַ֫חַשׂ","tr":"ya·cha·s","gloss":"genealogy","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"H4672","lemma":"מָצָא","tr":"ma·tsa","gloss":"to find","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":455},{"base":"H0902","lemma":"בִּגְוַי","tr":"big·vay","gloss":"Bigvai","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":6},{"base":"H5166","lemma":"נְחֶמְיָה","tr":"ne·chem·yah","gloss":"Nehemiah","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":8},{"base":"H1196","lemma":"בַּעֲנָה","tr":"ba·a·nah","gloss":"Baanah","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":9},{"base":"H2715","lemma":"חֹר","tr":"chor","gloss":"noble","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":13},{"base":"H5927","lemma":"עָלָה","tr":"a·lah","gloss":"to ascend: rise","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":889},{"base":"H5461","lemma":"סָגָן","tr":"sa·gan","gloss":"ruler","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":17},{"base":"H3187","lemma":"יָחַשׂ","tr":"ya·cha·s","gloss":"to enroll","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":18}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"EZR","chapter":2,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"accompanied by Zerubbabel, Jeshua, Nehemiah, Seraiah, Reelaiah, Mordecai, Bilshan, Mispar, Bigvai, Rehum, and Baanah. This is the count of the men of Israel:","from":7},{"book":"EZR","chapter":2,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"Now these are the people of the province who came up from the captivity of the exiles carried away to Babylon by Nebuchadnezzar its king. They returned to Jerusalem and Judah, each to his own town,","from":6},{"book":"EZR","chapter":2,"verse":70,"verseEnd":70,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"So the priests, the Levites, the singers, the gatekeepers, and the temple servants, along with some of the people, settled in their own towns; and the rest of the Israelites settled in their towns.","from":6},{"book":"EZR","chapter":5,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Let it be known to the king that we went into the province of Judah, to the house of the great God. The people are rebuilding it with large stones, and placing timbers in the walls. This work is being carried out diligently and is prospering in their hands.","from":6},{"book":"2KI","chapter":24,"verse":14,"verseEnd":16,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"He carried into exile all Jerusalem—all the commanders and mighty men of valor, all the craftsmen and metalsmiths—ten thousand captives in all. Only the poorest people of the land remained. Nebuchadnezzar carried away Jehoiachin to Babylon, as well as the kingʼs mother, his wives, his officials, and the leading men of the land. He took them into exile from Jerusalem to Babylon. The king of Babylon also brought into exile to Babylon all seven thousand men of valor and a thousand craftsmen and metalsmiths—all strong and fit for battle.","from":6},{"book":"2KI","chapter":25,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then Nebuzaradan captain of the guard carried into exile the people who remained in the city, along with the deserters who had defected to the king of Babylon and the rest of the population.","from":6},{"book":"1CH","chapter":9,"verse":1,"verseEnd":9,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"So all Israel was recorded in the genealogies written in the Book of the Kings of Israel. But Judah was exiled to Babylon because of their unfaithfulness. Now the first to resettle their own property in their cities were Israelites, priests, Levites, and temple servants. Some of the descendants of Judah, Benjamin, Ephraim, and Manasseh who lived in Jerusalem: Uthai son of Ammihud, the son of Omri, the son of Imri, the son of Bani, a descendant of Perez son of Judah. From the Shilonites: Asaiah the firstborn and his sons.","from":5},{"book":"2CH","chapter":36,"verse":1,"verseEnd":23,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then the people of the land took Jehoahaz son of Josiah and made him king in Jerusalem in place of his father. Jehoahaz was twenty-three years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem three months. And the king of Egypt dethroned him in Jerusalem and imposed on Judah a levy of a hundred talents of silver and a talent of gold. Then Neco king of Egypt made Eliakim brother of Jehoahaz king over Judah and Jerusalem, and he changed Eliakimʼs name to Jehoiakim. But Neco took Eliakimʼs brother Jehoahaz and carried him off to Egypt. Jehoiakim was twenty-five years old when he became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem eleven years. And he did evil in the sight of the LORD his God.","from":6}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"persian-era","title":"Persian era: Esther and the return","people":2},{"id":"royal-line","title":"The royal line: Judah to David to Jesus","people":2},{"i