,"uses":29},{"base":"H0505","lemma":"אֶ֫לֶף","tr":"e·leph","gloss":"thousand","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":506},{"base":"H7657","lemma":"שִׁבְעִים","tr":"shiv·im","gloss":"seventy","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":91},{"base":"H8083","lemma":"שְׁמֹנֶה","tr":"she·mo·neh","gloss":"eight","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":109},{"base":"H0705","lemma":"אַרְבָּעִים","tr":"ar·ba·im","gloss":"forty","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":135},{"base":"H8010","lemma":"שְׁלֹמֹה","tr":"she·lo·moh","gloss":"Solomon","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":293}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"LEV","chapter":27,"verse":2,"verseEnd":8,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"“Speak to the Israelites and say to them, ‘When someone makes a special vow to the LORD involving the value of persons, if the valuation concerns a male from twenty to sixty years of age, then your valuation shall be fifty shekels of silver, according to the sanctuary shekel. Or if it is a female, then your valuation shall be thirty shekels. And if the person is from five to twenty years of age, then your valuation for the male shall be twenty shekels, and for the female ten shekels. Now if the person is from one month to five years of age, then your valuation for the male shall be five shekels of silver, and for the female three shekels of silver.","from":46},{"book":"JOS","chapter":9,"verse":23,"verseEnd":27,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Now therefore you are under a curse and will perpetually serve as woodcutters and water carriers for the house of my God.” The Gibeonites answered, “Your servants were told clearly that the LORD your God had commanded His servant Moses to give you all the land and wipe out all its inhabitants before you. So we greatly feared for our lives because of you, and that is why we have done this. Now we are in your hands. Do to us whatever seems good and right to you.” So Joshua did this and delivered them from the hands of the Israelites, and they did not kill the Gibeonites. On that day he made them woodcutters and water carriers, as they are to this day for the congregation of the LORD and for the altar at the place He would choose.","from":46},{"book":"1CH","chapter":9,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Now the first to resettle their own property in their cities were Israelites, priests, Levites, and temple servants.","from":46},{"book":"1CH","chapter":9,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Adaiah son of Jeroham, the son of Pashhur, the son of Malchijah; Maasai son of Adiel, the son of Jahzerah, the son of Meshullam, the son of Meshillemith, the son of Immer;","from":41},{"book":"1CH","chapter":24,"verse":7,"verseEnd":19,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"The first lot fell to Jehoiarib, the second to Jedaiah, the third to Harim, the fourth to Seorim, the fifth to Malchijah, the sixth to Mijamin, the seventh to Hakkoz, the eighth to Abijah, the ninth to Jeshua, the tenth to Shecaniah,","from":39},{"book":"1CH","chapter":24,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"the third to Harim, the fourth to Seorim,","from":42},{"book":"1CH","chapter":24,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"the fifth to Malchijah, the sixth to Mijamin,","from":41},{"book":"1CH","chapter":24,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"the fifteenth to Bilgah, the sixteenth to Immer,","from":40}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"61-65":{"people":[{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":61},{"id":"delaiah-h1806i","name":"Delaiah","kind":"person","brief":"Returned from exile","count":1,"firstVerse":62},{"id":"nekoda-h5353h","name":"Nekoda","kind":"person","brief":"Returned priest","count":1,"firstVerse":62},{"id":"tobiah-h2900h","name":"Tobiah","kind":"person","brief":"Returned from exile","count":1,"firstVerse":62},{"id":"barzillai-h1271g","name":"Barzillai","kind":"person","brief":"David's compatriot","count":1,"firstVerse":63},{"id":"barzillai-h1271i","name":"Barzillai","kind":"person","brief":"Returned priest","count":1,"firstVerse":63},{"id":"habaiah-h2252","name":"Habaiah","kind":"person","brief":"Returned priest","count":1,"firstVerse":63},{"id":"hakkoz-h6976i","name":"Hakkoz","kind":"person","brief":"Returned priest","count":1,"firstVerse":63}],"places":[{"id":"addan-h0135","name":"Addan","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":61},{"id":"cherub-h3743","name":"Cherub","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":61},{"id":"immer-h0564i","name":"Immer","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":61},{"id":"tel-harsha-h8521","name":"Tel-harsha","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":61},{"id":"tel-melah-h8528","name":"Tel-melah","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":61},{"id":"gilead-h1568g","name":"Gilead","kind":"place","brief":"In Manasseh","count":1,"firstVerse":63}],"words":[{"base":"H8521","lemma":"תֵּל חַרְשָׁא","tr":"tel char·sah","gloss":"Tel-harsha","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":4},{"base":"H8528","lemma":"תֵּל מֶ֫לַח","tr":"tel me·lach","gloss":"Tel-melah","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":4},{"base":"H1271","lemma":"בַּרְזִלַּי","tr":"bar·zil·lay","gloss":"Barzillai","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":12},{"base":"H2252","lemma":"חֲבַיָה","tr":"cha·vay·yah","gloss":"Habaiah","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H3743","lemma":"כְּרוּב","tr":"ke·ruv","gloss":"Cherub","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H6944","lemma":"קֹ֫דֶשׁ","tr":"qo·desh","gloss":"holiness","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":469},{"base":"H5353","lemma":"נְקוֹדָא","tr":"ne·qo·da","gloss":"Nekoda","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"H8550","lemma":"תֻּמִּים","tr":"tum·mim","gloss":"Thummim","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":5},{"base":"H8660","lemma":"תִּרְשָׁתָא","tr":"tir·sha·ta","gloss":"governor","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":5},{"base":"H6976","lemma":"קוֹץ","tr":"qots","gloss":"Koz","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":6}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"EZR","chapter":2,"verse":59,"verseEnd":59,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"The following came up from Tel-melah, Tel-harsha, Cherub, Addan, and Immer, but they could not prove that their families were descended from Israel:","from":61},{"book":"EXO","chapter":28,"verse":30,"verseEnd":30,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"And place the Urim and Thummim in the breastpiece of judgment, so that they will also be over Aaronʼs heart whenever he comes before the LORD. Aaron will continually carry the judgment of the sons of Israel over his heart before the LORD.","from":65},{"book":"NEH","chapter":8,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Nehemiah the governor, Ezra the priest and scribe, and the Levites who were instructing the people said to all of them, “This day is holy to the LORD your God. Do not mourn or weep.” For all the people were weeping as they heard the words of the Law.","from":65},{"book":"LEV","chapter":2,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"The remainder of the grain offering shall belong to Aaron and his sons; it is a most holy part of the food offerings to the LORD.","from":65},{"book":"LEV","chapter":2,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"But the remainder of the grain offering shall belong to Aaron and his sons; it is a most holy part of the food offerings to the LORD.","from":65},{"book":"LEV","chapter":4,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"If the anointed priest sins, bringing guilt on the people, he must bring to the LORD a young bull without blemish as a sin offering for the sin he has committed.","from":64},{"book":"LEV","chapter":6,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"It must not be baked with leaven; I have assigned it as their portion of My food offerings. It is most holy, like the sin offering and the guilt offering.","from":65},{"book":"LEV","chapter":7,"verse":19,"verseEnd":20,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Meat that touches anything unclean must not be eaten; it is to be burned up. As for any other meat, anyone who is ceremonially clean may eat it. But if anyone who is unclean eats meat from the peace offering that belongs to the LORD, that person must be cut off from his people.","from":65}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"66-73":{"people":[{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":73},{"id":"levi-h3878","name":"Levi","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":73}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H3967","lemma":"מֵאָה","tr":"me·ah","gloss":"hundred","lang":"h","inPassage":9,"uses":581},{"base":"H1871","lemma":"דַּרְכְּמוֹן","tr":"dar·ke·mon","gloss":"drachma","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":4},{"base":"H0505","lemma":"אֶ֫לֶף","tr":"e·leph","gloss":"thousand","lang":"h","inPassage":6,"uses":506},{"base":"H7239","lemma":"רִבּוֹ","tr":"rib·bo","gloss":"ten thousand","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":10},{"base":"H7651","lemma":"שֶׁ֫בַע","tr":"she·va","gloss":"seven","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":394},{"base":"H7970","lemma":"שְׁלֹשִׁים","tr":"she·lo·shim","gloss":"thirty","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":172},{"base":"H7891","lemma":"שִׁיר","tr":"shir","gloss":"to sing","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":87},{"base":"H4488","lemma":"מָנֶה","tr":"ma·neh","gloss":"mina","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":5},{"base":"H2568","lemma":"חָמֵשׁ","tr":"cha·mesh","gloss":"five","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":343},{"base":"H3801","lemma":"כֻּתֹּ֫נֶת","tr":"ke·to·net","gloss":"tunic","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":29}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"EXO","chapter":12,"verse":22,"verseEnd":22,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Take a cluster of hyssop, dip it into the blood in the basin, and brush the blood on the top and sides of the doorframe. None of you shall go out the door of his house until morning.","from":70},{"book":"EXO","chapter":24,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Moses took half of the blood and put it in bowls, and the other half he splattered on the altar.","from":70},{"book":"NUM","chapter":7,"verse":2,"verseEnd":86,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And the leaders of Israel, the heads of their families, presented an offering. These men were the tribal leaders who had supervised the registration. They brought as their offering before the LORD six covered carts and twelve oxen—an ox from each leader and a cart from every two leaders—and presented them before the tabernacle. And the LORD said to Moses, “Accept these gifts from them, that they may be used in the work of the Tent of Meeting. And give them to the Levites, to each man according to his service.” So Moses took the carts and oxen and gave them to the Levites.","from":70},{"book":"1KI","chapter":7,"verse":45,"verseEnd":45,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"and the pots, shovels, and sprinkling bowls. All the articles that Huram made for King Solomon in the house of the LORD were made of burnished bronze.","from":70},{"book":"1CH","chapter":28,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"the weight of the pure gold for the forks, sprinkling bowls, and pitchers; the weight of each gold dish; the weight of each silver bowl;","from":70},{"book":"1CH","chapter":29,"verse":3,"verseEnd":9,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Moreover, because of my delight in the house of my God, I now give for it my personal treasures of gold and silver, over and above all that I have provided for this holy temple: three thousand talents of gold (the gold of Ophir) and seven thousand talents of refined silver, to overlay the walls of the buildings, for the gold work and the silver work, and for all the work to be done by the craftsmen. Now who is willing to consecrate himself to the LORD today?” Then the leaders of the families, the officers of the tribes of Israel, the commanders of thousands and of hundreds, and the officials in charge of the kingʼs work gave willingly. Toward the service of Godʼs house they gave 5,000 talents and 10,000 darics of gold, 10,000 talents of silver, 18,000 talents of bronze, and 100,000 talents of iron.","from":70},{"book":"2CH","chapter":4,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Additionally, he made ten tables and placed them in the temple, five on the south side and five on the north. He also made a hundred gold bowls.","from":70},{"book":"2CH","chapter":4,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Additionally, Huram made the pots, shovels, and sprinkling bowls. So Huram finished the work that he had undertaken for King Solomon in the house of God:","from":70}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2}]}}